        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski, thanks for quick reply!\r\n\r\n> I am afraid, this kind of functionality is a bit too much.\r\n\r\nI feel this is useful for big project with mixture of different languages, template files and nested subdirs. Like when i have 3 or more patterns it is more easy to be able to edit, than just to reset picker and write almost same from scratch again.\r\n\r\n> Especially since it requires so many new code.\r\n\r\nHalf of new code is taken from other `mini.nvim` modules (`H.user_input` and `H.echo` functions). I could use regular `vim.fn.input` and `print` but thought that using already written function is more stable approach. The rest of new code is like: get user input, check it and either remove or modify it. IMHO, it does not look like overkill functionality.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
